IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part8-assaults.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART VIII: sections 264 (criminal harassment), 264.1 (uttering threats), 265 to 269 (assaults),
-- 269.01 (aggravating circumstance: assault against a public transit employee) and 269.1 (torture). Imported by ccc8-part8-harm (s 263(3) names s 269).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING). Offences answer JUST TRUE or NOTHING (M1); a "when" / "where" / "if" condition that fails answers JUST FALSE (M2).
-- Answers taken from other sections enter as inputs named for them (`by s 2 bodily harm`, `by s 2 weapon`, `by s 2 peace officer`, `by s 2 public officer`, `by s 2 Canadian Forces`).
-- An offence named by section number (s 269.01(1)) is tested against the core `Provision of the Code`; for paragraph 264.1(1)(a) the `subsection` string is "(1)(a)" (assumed, not ruled).

§ `Section 264 -- Criminal harassment`

-- src:4930 | (2) The conduct mentioned in subsection (1) consists of doing any of the following in person, by a means of telecommunication or by any other means:
-- src:4931 | (a) repeatedly following from place to place the other person or anyone known to them;
-- src:4932 | (a.1) monitoring the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or of anyone known to them;
-- src:4933 | (b) repeatedly communicating with, either directly or indirectly, the other person or anyone known to them;
-- src:4934 | (c) besetting or watching the dwelling-house, or place where the other person, or anyone known to them, resides, works, carries on business or happens to be; or
-- src:4935 | (d) engaging in threatening conduct directed at the other person or at anyone or any animal known to them.
@ref s 264(2) (src:4930-4935)
GIVEN `the person repeatedly follows from place to place the other person or anyone known to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person monitors the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or of anyone known to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person repeatedly communicates with, either directly or indirectly, the other person or anyone known to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person besets or watches the dwelling-house, or place where the other person, or anyone known to them, resides, works, carries on business or happens to be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person engages in threatening conduct directed at the other person or at anyone or any animal known to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF     `the person repeatedly follows from place to place the other person or anyone known to them`
        OR `the person monitors the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or of anyone known to them`
        OR `the person repeatedly communicates with, either directly or indirectly, the other person or anyone known to them`
        OR `the person besets or watches the dwelling-house, or place where the other person, or anyone known to them, resides, works, carries on business or happens to be`
        OR `the person engages in threatening conduct directed at the other person or at anyone or any animal known to them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conduct mentioned in subsection (1) consists of doing any of the following in person, by a means of telecommunication or by any other means"

-- src:4947 | (6) For the purposes of this section, and for greater certainty, a person’s safety includes their psychological safety.
@ref s 264(6) (src:4947-4947)
GIVEN `the safety in question is the person's psychological safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(6) a person's safety includes their psychological safety` MEANS
    IF `the safety in question is the person's psychological safety`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a person's safety includes their psychological safety"

-- src:4928 | 264 (1) Everyone commits an offence who, with intent to harass another person or knowing that, or being reckless as to whether, they would be harassing another person, engages without lawful authority in conduct referred to in subsection (2) if, in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause that other person to believe that the other person’s safety, or the safety of anyone known to the other person, is threatened.
@ref s 264(1) (src:4928-4928)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to harass another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that they would be harassing another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reckless as to whether they would be harassing another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person engages in conduct referred to in subsection (2), by s 264(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person does so without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in all the circumstances the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause that other person to believe that the other person's safety, or the safety of anyone known to the other person, is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the mental element, conduct and lack of authority are met` AND `in all the circumstances the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause that other person to believe that the other person's safety, or the safety of anyone known to the other person, is threatened`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the mental element, conduct and lack of authority are met`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "engages without lawful authority in conduct referred to in subsection (2) if, in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause that other person to believe that the other person's safety ... is threatened" (an "if" condition: marginal reading M2)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone commits an offence who, with intent to harass another person or knowing that, or being reckless as to whether, they would be harassing another person, engages without lawful authority in conduct referred to in subsection (2)" (marginal reading M1)
    WHERE
        `the mental element, conduct and lack of authority are met` MEANS
                (`the person acts with intent to harass another person` OR `the person knows that they would be harassing another person` OR `the person is reckless as to whether they would be harassing another person`)
            AND `the person engages in conduct referred to in subsection (2), by s 264(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `the person does so without lawful authority`

-- src:4937 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under this section is
-- src:4938 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:4939 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 264(3) (src:4937-4939)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 264(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4938 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
@ref s 264(3)(a) (src:4938-4938)
`s 264(3)(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4937 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under this section is
-- src:4938 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:4939 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 264(3) (src:4937-4939)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 264(3) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 264(3)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4941 | (4) Where a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court imposing the sentence on the person shall consider as an aggravating factor that, at the time the offence was committed, the person contravened
-- src:4942 | (a) the terms or conditions of an order made under section 161 or a recognizance entered into under section 810, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2; or
-- src:4943 | (b) the terms or conditions of any other order or recognizance, or of an undertaking, made or entered into under the common law, this Act or any other Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature that is similar in effect to an order or recognizance referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref s 264(4) (src:4941-4943)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under section 264` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the offence was committed the person contravened the terms or conditions of an order made under section 161 or a recognizance entered into under section 810, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the offence was committed the person contravened the terms or conditions of any other order or recognizance, or of an undertaking, made or entered into under the common law, this Act or any other Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature that is similar in effect to an order or recognizance referred to in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(4) the court shall consider the contravention as an aggravating factor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is convicted of an offence under section 264`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court imposing the sentence on the person shall consider" (a "where" condition: marginal reading M2)
        IF `at the time the offence was committed the person contravened the terms or conditions of an order made under section 161 or a recognizance entered into under section 810, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` OR `at the time the offence was committed the person contravened the terms or conditions of any other order or recognizance, or of an undertaking, made or entered into under the common law, this Act or any other Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature that is similar in effect to an order or recognizance referred to in paragraph (a)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names the contravention of an order, recognizance or undertaking as the factor; for a conviction without one it says nothing

@ref s 264(4) (src:4941-4943)
DECLARE `s 264(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 264(4) consider the contravention as an aggravating factor`
    `s 264(5) give reasons for deciding not to give effect to the aggravating factor`

@ref s 264(4) (src:4941-4943)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 264(4) act`
`s 264(4) the duty of the court to consider the contravention` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 264(4) consider the contravention as an aggravating factor`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 264(4): the court did not consider the contravention as an aggravating factor"

-- src:4945 | (5) Where the court is satisfied of the existence of an aggravating factor referred to in subsection (4), but decides not to give effect to it for sentencing purposes, the court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref s 264(5) (src:4945-4945)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied of the existence of an aggravating factor referred to in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court decides not to give effect to it for sentencing purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(5) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied of the existence of an aggravating factor referred to in subsection (4)` AND `the court decides not to give effect to it for sentencing purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court is satisfied of the existence of an aggravating factor referred to in subsection (4), but decides not to give effect to it for sentencing purposes, the court shall give reasons for its decision" (a "where" condition: marginal reading M2)

@ref s 264(5) (src:4945-4945)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 264(4) act`
`s 264(5) the duty of the court to give reasons` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 264(5) give reasons for deciding not to give effect to the aggravating factor`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 264(5): the court did not give reasons for its decision not to give effect to the aggravating factor"

§ `Section 264.1 -- Uttering threats`

-- src:4951 | 264.1 (1) Every one commits an offence who, in any manner, knowingly utters, conveys or causes any person to receive a threat
-- src:4952 | (a) to cause death or bodily harm to any person;
-- src:4953 | (b) to burn, destroy or damage real or personal property; or
-- src:4954 | (c) to kill, poison or injure an animal or bird that is the property of any person.
@ref s 264.1(1) (src:4951-4954)
DECLARE `s 264.1(1) threat` IS ONE OF
    `s 264.1(1)(a) a threat to cause death or bodily harm to any person`
    `s 264.1(1)(b) a threat to burn, destroy or damage real or personal property`
    `s 264.1(1)(c) a threat to kill, poison or injure an animal or bird that is the property of any person`

@ref s 264.1(1) (src:4951-4954)
GIVEN threat IS A `s 264.1(1) threat`
      `the person, in any manner, knowingly utters, conveys or causes any person to receive the threat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.1(1) the person commits the offence of uttering threats` MEANS
    IF `the person, in any manner, knowingly utters, conveys or causes any person to receive the threat`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone commits an offence who, in any manner, knowingly utters, conveys or causes any person to receive a threat (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..." (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 264.1(1) (src:4951-4954)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 264.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4957 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
@ref s 264.1(2)(a) (src:4957-4957)
`s 264.1(2)(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4961 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
@ref s 264.1(3)(a) (src:4961-4961)
`s 264.1(3)(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4956 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under paragraph (1)(a) is guilty of
-- src:4957 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:4958 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 264.1(2) (src:4956-4958)
GIVEN threat IS A `s 264.1(1) threat`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 264.1 the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER threat
    WHEN `s 264.1(1)(a) a threat to cause death or bodily harm to any person` THEN LIST `s 264.1(2)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN `s 264.1(1)(b) a threat to burn, destroy or damage real or personal property` THEN LIST `s 264.1(3)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN `s 264.1(1)(c) a threat to kill, poison or injure an animal or bird that is the property of any person` THEN LIST `s 264.1(3)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 265 -- Assault`

-- src:4971 | (3) For the purposes of this section, no consent is obtained where the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of
-- src:4972 | (a) the application of force to the complainant or to a person other than the complainant;
-- src:4973 | (b) threats or fear of the application of force to the complainant or to a person other than the complainant;
-- src:4974 | (c) fraud; or
-- src:4975 | (d) the exercise of authority.
@ref s 265(3) (src:4971-4975)
GIVEN `the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of the application of force to the complainant or to a person other than the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of threats or fear of the application of force to the complainant or to a person other than the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of the exercise of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265(3) no consent is obtained` MEANS
    IF `the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of the application of force to the complainant or to a person other than the complainant` OR `the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of threats or fear of the application of force to the complainant or to a person other than the complainant` OR `the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of fraud` OR `the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of the exercise of authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "no consent is obtained where the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of (a) ... (d)" (the text says when no consent is obtained, not that consent is obtained in every other case)

-- src:4964 | 265 (1) A person commits an assault when
-- src:4965 | (a) without the consent of another person, he applies force intentionally to that other person, directly or indirectly;
-- src:4966 | (b) he attempts or threatens, by an act or a gesture, to apply force to another person, if he has, or causes that other person to believe on reasonable grounds that he has, present ability to effect his purpose; or
-- src:4967 | (c) while openly wearing or carrying a weapon or an imitation thereof, he accosts or impedes another person or begs.
@ref s 265(1) (src:4964-4967)
GIVEN `the person applies force intentionally to another person, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no consent is obtained, by s 265(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person attempts or threatens, by an act or a gesture, to apply force to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has present ability to effect his purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causes that other person to believe on reasonable grounds that he has present ability to effect his purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is openly wearing or carrying a weapon or an imitation thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person accosts or impedes another person or begs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265(1) the person commits an assault` MEANS
    IF     (`the person applies force intentionally to another person, directly or indirectly` AND ((NOT `the other person consents`) OR `no consent is obtained, by s 265(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
        OR (`the person attempts or threatens, by an act or a gesture, to apply force to another person` AND (`the person has present ability to effect his purpose` OR `the person causes that other person to believe on reasonable grounds that he has present ability to effect his purpose`))
        OR (`the person is openly wearing or carrying a weapon or an imitation thereof` AND `the person accosts or impedes another person or begs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an assault when (a) without the consent of another person, he applies force intentionally ...; (b) he attempts or threatens, by an act or a gesture, to apply force to another person, if he has, or causes that other person to believe on reasonable grounds that he has, present ability to effect his purpose; or (c) while openly wearing or carrying a weapon or an imitation thereof, he accosts or impedes another person or begs" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4969 | (2) This section applies to all forms of assault, including sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm and aggravated sexual assault.
@ref s 265(2) (src:4969-4969)
GIVEN `it is a form of assault, including sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm, or aggravated sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265(2) section 265 applies to the form of assault` MEANS
    IF `it is a form of assault, including sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm, or aggravated sexual assault`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "This section applies to all forms of assault, including sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm and aggravated sexual assault"

-- src:4977 | (4) Where an accused alleges that he believed that the complainant consented to the conduct that is the subject-matter of the charge, a judge, if satisfied that there is sufficient evidence and that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence, shall instruct the jury, when reviewing all the evidence relating to the determination of the honesty of the accused’s belief, to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for that belief.
@ref s 265(4) (src:4977-4977)
GIVEN `the accused alleges that he believed that the complainant consented to the conduct that is the subject-matter of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there is sufficient evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265(4) the judge shall instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief` MEANS
    IF `the accused alleges that he believed that the complainant consented to the conduct that is the subject-matter of the charge` AND `the judge is satisfied that there is sufficient evidence` AND `the judge is satisfied that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused alleges that he believed that the complainant consented ..., a judge, if satisfied that there is sufficient evidence and that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence, shall instruct the jury" (a "where" / "if" condition: marginal reading M2)

@ref s 265(4) (src:4977-4977)
DECLARE `s 265(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 265(4) instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief`

@ref s 265(4) (src:4977-4977)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 265(4) act`
`s 265(4) the duty of the judge to instruct the jury` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 265(4) instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "s 265(4): the jury was not instructed to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief"

§ `Sections 266 to 269 -- Assault, with a weapon or causing bodily harm, aggravated assault, unlawfully causing bodily harm`

-- src:4979 | 266 Every one who commits an assault is guilty of
-- src:4980 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:4981 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 266 (src:4979-4981)
GIVEN `the person commits an assault, by s 265(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 266 the person commits the offence of assault` MEANS
    IF `the person commits an assault, by s 265(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who commits an assault is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 266 (src:4979-4981)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 266 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 266(a) (src:4980-4980)
`s 266(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 266 (src:4979-4981)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 266 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 266(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4983 | 267 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, in committing an assault,
-- src:4984 | (a) carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon or an imitation thereof,
-- src:4985 | (b) causes bodily harm to the complainant, or
-- src:4986 | (c) chokes, suffocates or strangles the complainant.
@ref s 267 (src:4983-4986)
GIVEN `the person commits an assault, by s 265(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in committing it the person carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon, by s 2 weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in committing it the person carries, uses or threatens to use an imitation of a weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in committing it the person causes bodily harm to the complainant, by s 2 bodily harm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in committing it the person chokes, suffocates or strangles the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267 the person commits the offence of assault with a weapon or causing bodily harm` MEANS
    IF     `the person commits an assault, by s 265(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (   `in committing it the person carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon, by s 2 weapon` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `in committing it the person carries, uses or threatens to use an imitation of a weapon`
            OR `in committing it the person causes bodily harm to the complainant, by s 2 bodily harm` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `in committing it the person chokes, suffocates or strangles the complainant`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... or ... summary conviction who, in committing an assault, (a) carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon or an imitation thereof, (b) causes bodily harm to the complainant, or (c) chokes, suffocates or strangles the complainant" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 267 (src:4983-4986)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 267 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 267 (src:4983-4986)
`s 267 the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 267 (src:4983-4986)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 267 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 267 the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4992 | (3) For greater certainty, in this section, “wounds” or “maims” includes to excise, infibulate or mutilate, in whole or in part, the labia majora, labia minora or clitoris of a person, except where
-- src:4993 | (a) a surgical procedure is performed, by a person duly qualified by provincial law to practise medicine, for the benefit of the physical health of the person or for the purpose of that person having normal reproductive functions or normal sexual appearance or function; or
-- src:4994 | (b) the person is at least eighteen years of age and there is no resulting bodily harm.
@ref s 268(3) (src:4992-4994)
GIVEN `it is to excise, infibulate or mutilate, in whole or in part, the labia majora, labia minora or clitoris of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a surgical procedure is performed, by a person duly qualified by provincial law to practise medicine, for the benefit of the physical health of the person or for the purpose of that person having normal reproductive functions or normal sexual appearance or function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is at least eighteen years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no resulting bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(3) "wounds" or "maims" includes the excision, infibulation or mutilation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is to excise, infibulate or mutilate, in whole or in part, the labia majora, labia minora or clitoris of a person` AND (`a surgical procedure is performed, by a person duly qualified by provincial law to practise medicine, for the benefit of the physical health of the person or for the purpose of that person having normal reproductive functions or normal sexual appearance or function` OR (`the person is at least eighteen years of age` AND `there is no resulting bodily harm`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "includes to excise, infibulate or mutilate ... except where (a) a surgical procedure is performed ... or (b) the person is at least eighteen years of age and there is no resulting bodily harm"
        IF `it is to excise, infibulate or mutilate, in whole or in part, the labia majora, labia minora or clitoris of a person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "'wounds' or 'maims' includes"

-- src:4988 | 268 (1) Every one commits an aggravated assault who wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant.
@ref s 268(1) (src:4988-4988)
GIVEN `the person wounds or maims the complainant, including by an act described in s 268(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person disfigures the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person endangers the life of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(1) the person commits an aggravated assault` MEANS
    IF `the person wounds or maims the complainant, including by an act described in s 268(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person disfigures the complainant` OR `the person endangers the life of the complainant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits an aggravated assault who wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant" (marginal reading M1)

-- src:4990 | (2) Every one who commits an aggravated assault is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 268(2) (src:4990-4990)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 268(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 268(2) (src:4990-4990)
`s 268(2) the limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 268(2) (src:4990-4990)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 268(2) the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 268(2) the limb`

-- src:4996 | (4) For the purposes of this section and section 265, no consent to the excision, infibulation or mutilation, in whole or in part, of the labia majora, labia minora or clitoris of a person is valid, except in the cases described in paragraphs (3)(a) and (b).
@ref s 268(4) (src:4996-4996)
GIVEN `the consent is to the excision, infibulation or mutilation, in whole or in part, of the labia majora, labia minora or clitoris of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a case described in paragraph (3)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(4) the consent is valid` MEANS
    IF `the consent is to the excision, infibulation or mutilation, in whole or in part, of the labia majora, labia minora or clitoris of a person` AND (NOT `it is a case described in paragraph (3)(a) or (b)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no consent to the excision, infibulation or mutilation ... is valid, except in the cases described in paragraphs (3)(a) and (b)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in the cases described in paragraphs (3)(a) and (b)" (the text does not say that consent is valid in those cases)

-- src:5000 | (2) In this section, sterilization procedure means the severing, clipping, tying or cauterizing, in whole or in part, of the Fallopian tubes, ovaries or uterus of a person or any other procedure performed on a person that results in the permanent prevention of reproduction, regardless of whether the procedure is reversible through a subsequent surgical procedure.
@ref s 268.1(2) (src:5000-5000)
GIVEN `it is the severing, clipping, tying or cauterizing, in whole or in part, of the Fallopian tubes, ovaries or uterus of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is any other procedure performed on a person that results in the permanent prevention of reproduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268.1(2) sterilization procedure` MEANS
    -- "regardless of whether the procedure is reversible through a subsequent surgical procedure": that fact makes no difference, so the function takes none.
    IF `it is the severing, clipping, tying or cauterizing, in whole or in part, of the Fallopian tubes, ovaries or uterus of a person` OR `it is any other procedure performed on a person that results in the permanent prevention of reproduction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sterilization procedure means the severing, clipping, tying or cauterizing, in whole or in part, of the Fallopian tubes, ovaries or uterus of a person or any other procedure performed on a person that results in the permanent prevention of reproduction"

-- src:4998 | 268.1 (1) For greater certainty, a sterilization procedure is an act that wounds or maims a person for the purposes of subsection 268(1).
@ref s 268.1(1) (src:4998-4998)
GIVEN `the act is a sterilization procedure, by s 268.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268.1(1) the act wounds or maims a person for the purposes of subsection 268(1)` MEANS
    IF `the act is a sterilization procedure, by s 268.1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a sterilization procedure is an act that wounds or maims a person for the purposes of subsection 268(1)" (the text says nothing of other acts)

-- src:5002 | 269 Every one who unlawfully causes bodily harm to any person is guilty of
-- src:5003 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:5004 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 269 (src:5002-5004)
GIVEN `the person unlawfully causes bodily harm to any person, by s 2 bodily harm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269 the person commits the offence of unlawfully causing bodily harm` MEANS
    IF `the person unlawfully causes bodily harm to any person, by s 2 bodily harm` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who unlawfully causes bodily harm to any person is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 269 (src:5002-5004)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 269 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 269(a) (src:5003-5003)
`s 269(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 269 (src:5002-5004)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 269 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 269(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 269.01 -- Aggravating circumstance: assault against a public transit employee`

-- src:5009 | public transit employee means an individual who works for, or is contracted to work for, an organization that provides passenger transportation services to the public. (employé des services de transport en commun)
@ref s 269.01(2) public transit employee (src:5009-5009)
GIVEN `it is an individual who works for, or is contracted to work for, an organization that provides passenger transportation services to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269.01(2) public transit employee` MEANS
    IF `it is an individual who works for, or is contracted to work for, an organization that provides passenger transportation services to the public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "public transit employee means an individual who works for, or is contracted to work for, an organization that provides passenger transportation services to the public"

-- src:5010 | vehicle includes a bus, paratransit vehicle, licensed taxi cab, train, subway, tram and ferry. (véhicule)
@ref s 269.01(2) vehicle (src:5010-5010)
GIVEN `it is a bus, paratransit vehicle, licensed taxi cab, train, subway, tram or ferry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269.01(2) vehicle` MEANS
    IF `it is a bus, paratransit vehicle, licensed taxi cab, train, subway, tram or ferry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "vehicle includes a bus, paratransit vehicle, licensed taxi cab, train, subway, tram and ferry"

-- src:5006 | 269.01 (1) When a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in paragraph 264.1(1)(a) or any of sections 266 to 269, it shall consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the victim of the offence was, at the time of the commission of the offence, a public transit employee engaged in the performance of his or her duty.
@ref s 269.01(1) (src:5006-5006)
GIVEN `the offence the court imposes a sentence for` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the victim was, at the time of the commission of the offence, a public transit employee, by s 269.01(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the victim was engaged in the performance of his or her duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269.01(1) the court shall consider the fact as an aggravating circumstance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offence is one referred to`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in paragraph 264.1(1)(a) or any of sections 266 to 269, it shall consider" (a "when" condition: marginal reading M2)
        IF `the victim was, at the time of the commission of the offence, a public transit employee, by s 269.01(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the victim was engaged in the performance of his or her duty` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the fact that the victim of the offence was, at the time of the commission of the offence, a public transit employee engaged in the performance of his or her duty"
    WHERE
        `the offence is one referred to` MEANS
               (`the offence the court imposes a sentence for`'s `section` EQUALS 264.1 AND `the offence the court imposes a sentence for`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)(a)")
            OR elem (`the offence the court imposes a sentence for`'s `section`) (LIST 266, 267, 268, 269)

@ref s 269.01(1) (src:5006-5006)
DECLARE `s 269.01(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 269.01(1) consider the fact that the victim was a public transit employee as an aggravating circumstance`

@ref s 269.01(1) (src:5006-5006)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 269.01(1) act`
`s 269.01(1) the duty of the court to consider the aggravating circumstance` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 269.01(1) consider the fact that the victim was a public transit employee as an aggravating circumstance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 269.01(1): the court did not consider the fact that the victim was a public transit employee as an aggravating circumstance"

§ `Section 269.1 -- Torture`

-- src:5015 | official means
-- src:5016 | (a) a peace officer,
-- src:5017 | (b) a public officer,
-- src:5018 | (c) a member of the Canadian Forces, or
-- src:5019 | (d) any person who may exercise powers, pursuant to a law in force in a foreign state, that would, in Canada, be exercised by a person referred to in paragraph (a), (b), or (c),
-- src:5020 | whether the person exercises powers in Canada or outside Canada; (fonctionnaire)
@ref s 269.1(2) official (src:5015-5020)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the Canadian Forces, by s 2 Canadian Forces` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person may exercise powers, pursuant to a law in force in a foreign state, that would, in Canada, be exercised by a person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269.1(2) official` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person is a member of the Canadian Forces, by s 2 Canadian Forces` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person may exercise powers, pursuant to a law in force in a foreign state, that would, in Canada, be exercised by a person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- "whether the person exercises powers in Canada or outside Canada": that fact makes no difference, so the function takes none
        IF `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the person is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the person is a member of the Canadian Forces, by s 2 Canadian Forces` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an answer of section 2 is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "official means (a) a peace officer, (b) a public officer, (c) a member of the Canadian Forces, or (d) any person who may exercise powers, pursuant to a law in force in a foreign state"

-- src:5021 | torture means any act or omission by which severe pain or suffering, whether physical or mental, is intentionally inflicted on a person
-- src:5022 | (a) for a purpose including
-- src:5023 | (i) obtaining from the person or from a third person information or a statement,
-- src:5024 | (ii) punishing the person for an act that the person or a third person has committed or is suspected of having committed, and
-- src:5025 | (iii) intimidating or coercing the person or a third person, or
-- src:5026 | (b) for any reason based on discrimination of any kind,
-- src:5027 | but does not include any act or omission arising only from, inherent in or incidental to lawful sanctions. (torture)
@ref s 269.1(2) torture (src:5021-5027)
GIVEN `severe pain or suffering, whether physical or mental, is intentionally inflicted on a person by an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for a purpose including obtaining from the person or from a third person information or a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for a purpose including punishing the person for an act that the person or a third person has committed or is suspected of having committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for a purpose including intimidating or coercing the person or a third person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for any reason based on discrimination of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission arises only from, is inherent in or incidental to lawful sanctions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269.1(2) torture` MEANS
    IF     `severe pain or suffering, whether physical or mental, is intentionally inflicted on a person by an act or omission`
       AND (   `it is for a purpose including obtaining from the person or from a third person information or a statement`
            OR `it is for a purpose including punishing the person for an act that the person or a third person has committed or is suspected of having committed`
            OR `it is for a purpose including intimidating or coercing the person or a third person`
            OR `it is for any reason based on discrimination of any kind`)
       AND (NOT `the act or omission arises only from, is inherent in or incidental to lawful sanctions`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "torture means any act or omission by which severe pain or suffering, whether physical or mental, is intentionally inflicted on a person (a) for a purpose including ... or (b) for any reason based on discrimination of any kind, but does not include any act or omission arising only from, inherent in or incidental to lawful sanctions"

-- src:5012 | 269.1 (1) Every official, or every person acting at the instigation of or with the consent or acquiescence of an official, who inflicts torture on any other person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 269.1(1) (src:5012-5012)
GIVEN `the person is an official, by s 269.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acts at the instigation of or with the consent or acquiescence of an official` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person inflicts torture on any other person, by s 269.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269.1(1) the person commits the offence of torture` MEANS
    IF (`the person is an official, by s 269.1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person acts at the instigation of or with the consent or acquiescence of an official`) AND `the person inflicts torture on any other person, by s 269.1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every official, or every person acting at the instigation of or with the consent or acquiescence of an official, who inflicts torture on any other person is guilty of an indictable offence" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 269.1(1) (src:5012-5012)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 269.1(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 269.1(1) (src:5012-5012)
`s 269.1(1) the limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 269.1(1) (src:5012-5012)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 269.1(1) the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 269.1(1) the limb`

-- src:5029 | (3) It is no defence to a charge under this section that the accused was ordered by a superior or a public authority to perform the act or omission that forms the subject-matter of the charge or that the act or omission is alleged to have been justified by exceptional circumstances, including a state of war, a threat of war, internal political instability or any other public emergency.
@ref s 269.1(3) (src:5029-5029)
GIVEN `the accused was ordered by a superior or a public authority to perform the act or omission that forms the subject-matter of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is alleged to have been justified by exceptional circumstances, including a state of war, a threat of war, internal political instability or any other public emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269.1(3) the circumstance is a defence to a charge under this section` MEANS
    IF `the accused was ordered by a superior or a public authority to perform the act or omission that forms the subject-matter of the charge` OR `the act or omission is alleged to have been justified by exceptional circumstances, including a state of war, a threat of war, internal political instability or any other public emergency`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is no defence to a charge under this section that the accused was ordered by a superior or a public authority to perform the act or omission ... or that the act or omission is alleged to have been justified by exceptional circumstances"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names two circumstances that are no defence and says nothing of any other

-- src:5031 | (4) In any proceedings over which Parliament has jurisdiction, any statement obtained as a result of the commission of an offence under this section is inadmissible in evidence, except as evidence that the statement was so obtained.
@ref s 269.1(4) (src:5031-5031)
GIVEN `the statement was obtained as a result of the commission of an offence under section 269.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in proceedings over which Parliament has jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is tendered as evidence that the statement was so obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269.1(4) the statement is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the statement was obtained as a result of the commission of an offence under section 269.1` AND `it is in proceedings over which Parliament has jurisdiction` AND (NOT `it is tendered as evidence that the statement was so obtained`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any statement obtained as a result of the commission of an offence under this section is inadmissible in evidence, except as evidence that the statement was so obtained"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except as evidence that the statement was so obtained" (the text does not say the statement is admissible for that purpose) and the rule applies only "in any proceedings over which Parliament has jurisdiction"
